+\caption{Q4 per market: B3 minus R3 gain difference and its calibrated lower bound, R3's efficiency and lower bound, the raw one-sided bootstrap $p$-values of the two components, the calibrated market value $\max(p'_{\mathrm{gain}}, p'_{\mathrm{eff}})$ that enters Holm, its Holm-adjusted value, and the decision. The decisions on fresh0, fresh1, fresh3, and fresh4 are about the prescribed search procedure; the Decision column marks the direct flags (fresh1, fresh4) and the flags fresh0 and fresh3 inherit through their references (addendum).}\label{tab:q4}
+\end{table}
+
+\begin{figure}[t]\centering
+\includegraphics[width=0.7\linewidth]{figures/fig_q4.pdf}
+\caption{Q4: per-market lower bounds against the registered thresholds.}\label{fig:q4}
+\end{figure}
+
+\paragraph{Which parts of R3 matter (Q2).} Under separately searched D2+H3 attacks, pooled over the fresh markets, the main effects on the gain are \site{r_q2_p} for the priority phase P and \site{r_q2_g} for newest-first residual targeting G, both reductions, and \site{r_q2_s} for pacing S, a small increase (X7-SC: \site{r_q2_s_x}). The two targeting parts are substitutes: the PG factorial contrast, half the difference between G's conditional effects, is \site{r_q2_pg}; G changes the gain by \site{r_q2_g_p0} without the priority phase and by only \site{r_q2_g_p1} with it, and the priority phase changes it by only \site{r_q2_p_g1} once G is in place, so given newest-first targeting the priority phase is close to redundant in this model. In the pooled contrasts, either P or G alone accounts for most of the measured reduction; adding the other contributes little. The pattern also appears in the fixed-attack contrasts averaged over the eight selected attacks (P: \site{r_q2_fixed_p}). Our registered conjectures (P negligible, the targeting parts additive, S helpful) failed as scored (Table~\ref{tab:predictions}); the stricter eligibility reading of Table~\ref{tab:pred-eligibility} leaves them not assessed, with the estimates unchanged. X7-SC agrees (Table~\ref{tab:q2-x7sc}).
+
+\begin{table}[t]\centering\small
+\adjustbox{max width=\linewidth}{\input{tables/q2_d2h3.tex}}
+\caption{Q2 under D2+H3: factorial contrasts, searched and fixed attacks, with attack and reference terms and efficiency (descriptive, nominal intervals).}\label{tab:q2}
+\end{table}
