   259	\adjustbox{max width=\linewidth}{\input{tables/posthoc_welfare_mix.tex}}
   260	\caption{Exploratory, after the report: at the headline market, the efficiency of the selected W1 and W0 attacks, and, for each companion family, the episode-level lottery between the W0 attack and a profitable attack of the same rule (two displayed companions, H4 and D2+H3; all five examined companions are in \texttt{posthoc.json}) at the largest W0 weight on a grid of step \const{0.0005} whose mean gain keeps a non-negative nominal one-sided \const{95} percent lower bound, unadjusted for selection; estimated gain, that bound, and the mixture's efficiency, all on the evaluation records that selected the weight; ``Train gain'' is the mixture's mean gain on the training seeds (the registered W1 constraint requires it to be non-negative), reconstructed from the search archives. The row marked training-feasible, added after external review, uses the largest grid weight at which both the evaluation bound and the training gain are non-negative. B3's W0 attack has a positive estimated gain.}\label{tab:ph-welfare}

